RF.put("questb:b57",{"8697":{"id":8697,"t":"Ring of Infinite Wisdom","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Ceremonial Ring, 2 Obsidian Idols, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Ceremonial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Obsidian Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nRing of Infinite Wisdom\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gem on the ring for you. You'll find the effect is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8617":{"id":8617,"t":"The horde needs singed corestones","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Bring 50 singed corestones to General Zog in Durotar.\n50 Singed Corestone","desc":"The time has come for you to contribute to the Ahn'Qiraj war effort, ‹class›. Gone are the halcyon days of whiling away your time in leisure. Now it is time to serve me and the Horde, and I assure you that I am not as forgiving as the Warchief.\nYou will gather your forces, a guild if you have one, and invade the Molten Core. Inside you will find that the denizens of the place have singed corestones. Bring these back to me in large quantities.\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Type Raid Shareable Yes Quest ID 8617","cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"537":{"id":537,"t":"Dark Council","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 4 Argus Shadow Mages.\nBring the Head of Nagaz to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\nHead of Nagaz Nagaz\nArgus Shadow Mage slain : 0/ 4","desc":"The letter you brought me was written by a being who calls himself Nagaz, a member of the Argus Wake. I don't know what this Argus Wake is, but if they're in alliance with the Syndicate then they must be a threat.\nI want you to find Nagaz and the Argus Shadow Mages mentioned in that letter. I want you to find them, and kill them.\nSearch in the Uplands, where the Syndicate is strongest. It is north of Strahnbrad.\nWith luck, you'll find these envoys of the Argus Wake there.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you find the envoys of The Argus Wake?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. The Argus Wake does not sound like a group we want running the Syndicate.\nAnd although you may have destroyed their leader here, Nagaz was merely the servant of another. The Argus Wake might run deep through the continent of Azeroth.\nOr even the world.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":48.1,"y":59.1,"n":"Magistrate Henry Maleb","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8297":{"id":8297,"t":"Arathi Basin Resources!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you. They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!\nThat is why Arathi Basin is important. There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources. Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.\nThat is what I want from you, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Do you have the resource crate, ‹name›? The League of Arathor can't fight a decent battle without them...","done":"You got the resources! Great job! I'll send the resources to our quartermasters, who can quickly disperse them to our troops.\nThank you, ‹name›. Indeed, performing successful missions like the one you achieved are how wars are truly won.\nLevel 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8297","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"697":{"id":697,"t":"Malin's Request","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sealed Letter to Archmage Malin in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\nSealed Letter to Archmage Malin\nProvided: Sealed Letter to Archmage Malin","desc":"Take this letter back to Stormwind and let Malin know that Kryten an' I'll be home soon. He'll reward you well for helping us here, ‹name›, of that I've no doubt.\nTravel safely.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nVigilant Buckler Wingborne Boots\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,750\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes? You look vaguely familiar. I do apologize, but have we met? I get so busy I lose track.","done":"<Archmage Malin opens the letter, and his eyes grow wide.>\nBy the Light, you've done it. How wonderful. Trelane will be so pleased. I'm sure Kryten and Skuerto are just as excited as I am to have them on their way back to Stormwind.\nThank you, ‹name›. Please, take this to help you in your journeys.\nArathi Highlands Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.7,"y":47,"n":"Skuerto","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":87.5,"n":"Archmage Malin","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1017":{"id":1017,"t":"Mage Summoner","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Sarilus Foulborne and bring his head to Sentinel Velene Starstrike in Silverwind Refuge.\nSarilus Foulborne's Head Sarilus Foulborne","desc":"There's only one undead mage in the Barrens capable of defiling this many water elementals. He's also the only one foolish enough to try. Sarilus Foulborne is probably sitting at the top of Dreadmist Peak, laughing at me.\n‹name›, you must go into enemy territory and destroy this miscreant. I have had enough of his idiocy and we must show him what happens to those who annoy the Sentinels.\nDestroy him and bring me his head. Be wary though, the Horde may be watching for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nLight of Elune\nExperience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Is it done? Is Sarilus Foulborne dead?","done":"Now I can see that repugnant smile wiped from his face forever. You have done very well, ‹name›. Take this, the Light of Elune, drink of it when all seems lost and death is near. It may save you, Goddess willing.\nAshenvale The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":49.8,"y":67.2,"n":"Sentinel Velene Starstrike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"777":{"id":777,"t":"This Is Going to Be Hard","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Cog #5 to Lotwil Veriatus.\nCog #5\nProvided: Cog #5","desc":"Okay, here you go.\nI'm going to be over here... behind cover.\nFeel free to join me.","back":"<Without looking up from the shackles, Lotwil holds out a hand and waggles his fingers impatiently.>\nThe cog, ‹name›, the cog!","done":"Ah, perfect. Stand back while I prepare to make more history!\n<Lotwil continues to work feverishly.>","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Lucien Tosselwrench","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"7657":{"id":7657,"t":"Imperial Plate Helm","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"50 Thorium Bar","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Imperial Plate Helm\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"Just hand over 50 thorium bars and the helm plans are yers.","done":"A pleasure doin' business with ya.\nAnd ‹name›, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.7,"n":"Derotain Mudsipper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"96057":{"id":96057,"t":"Camping 101 tailoring","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Uthrar Threx in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your tailoring skill to 20","desc":"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nDun Morogh Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":43.6,"y":28.2,"n":"Uthrar Threx","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"92457":{"id":92457,"t":"Starving arcane","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat 8 Seeking Remnants, 8 Saturated Remnants, and 8 Mana Echoes inside the City of Dalaran for Archmage Modera outside of Dalaran.\nSeeking Remnant slain : 0/ 8\nSaturated Remnant slain : 0/ 8\nMana Echo slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The breach has affected many of our factotums and enchantments throughout the city, including many that are seeing to our defenses. This fragmented arcane energy has spoken to rogue elementals who seek to saturate themselves in this free flowing magic.\nWhile we are busy tending to the wards and other major incidents, it would be a favor to the Kirin Tor if you could cull this elemental throng.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFallen Guard's Pendant Arcane Infused Rod\nExperience: 9,400\n+100 reputation with Kirin Tor\nLevel 33 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 29 31 36 42 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 92457","cats":["city-of-dalaran"]},"94217":{"id":94217,"t":"Craftsmans writ lesser trolls blood elixir","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir\nLesser Troll's Blood Elixir","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Yarr, you be bringin' me my elixir?","done":"Exactly what Short John Mithril ordered!\nHere's ye' coin. I'd keep it clutched to your chest as ye' scuttle out of here, the arena combatants thirst for riches as much as they thirst for blood!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":29.6,"y":47.4,"n":"Short John Mithril","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94297":{"id":94297,"t":"Craftsmans writ quickdraw quiver","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Quickdraw Quiver\nQuickdraw Quiver","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Quickdraw Quiver, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Quickdraw Quiver Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94297","cats":["crafting"]},"7897":{"id":7897,"t":"Mechanical Repair Kits","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"6 Mechanical Repair Kit","rew":"You will receive:\n12 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"The biggest reason I can't open up my booth is that... everything's broken! I need mechanical repair kits to fix all this stuff!\nCan you bring me those kits, ‹name›? I'll trade you... kits for Darkmoon Faire tickets. What do you say?","done":"Thank you! Now I can get to fixing things.\nIt's going to take a lot of repair kits and a lot of late nights to get everything in working order. Sometimes I think it'd be better to get back to my roots and restart my career as a headhunter, but... the Faire has been good to me.\nTake these tickets, ‹name›, and have fun!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38,"y":44.3,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":70.7,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"96137":{"id":96137,"t":"Iras dagger","lv":24,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat 10 Young Black Ravagers and 7 Black Ravagers then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.\nYoung Black Ravager slain : 0/ 10\nBlack Ravager slain : 0/ 7\nProvided: Ira's Dagger","desc":"A small dagger belonging to the self-appointed ranger, Ira, who kept the forests safe by preventing the beasts within from attacking travelers.\nWith Ira's spirit still wandering the woods, perhaps her unfinished business was to clear out the worg that continue to claim victims throughout the forest.\nDuskwood Open the zone on the world map Start an item: Ira's Dagger Level 24 , requires level 18 Difficulty 18 20 22 27 32 Side Alliance Quest ID 96137","cats":["duskwood"]},"57":{"id":57,"t":"The Night Watch","lv":26,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke of Darkshire wants you to kill 15 Skeletal Fiends and 15 Skeletal Horrors.\nSkeletal Fiend slain : 0/ 15\nSkeletal Horror slain : 0/ 15","desc":"‹name›, I'm getting reports of an undead infestation in the forest! If you're up to the job, journey to the Raven Hill graveyard and slay 15 of those vile Skeletal Fiends and 15 Skeletal Horrors. There are also reports of skeletons just south of Darkshire, in and around Tranquil Gardens Cemetery. The undead must be driven from Duskwood!","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Return to me once you have killed 15 Skeletal Fiends and 15 Skeletal Horrors, ‹name›.","done":"The people of Darkshire thank you, ‹name›. You have proven yourself to be a great ally of The Night Watch.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1177":{"id":1177,"t":"Hungry!","lv":36,"min":32,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mudcrush Durtfeet in northern Dustwallow wants 8 Mirefin Heads.\n8 Mirefin Head Mirefin Oracle 33 % , Mirefin Coastrunner 33 % , Mirefin Muckdweller 33 % , Mirefin Warrior 33 % and 3 more","desc":"Mud big ogre.\nMe hungry.\nGo bash fishy. Bring Mud food.\nYou feed Mud or Mud eat you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMud's Crushers Durtfeet Stompers\nExperience: 2,800","back":"Gimme food or me eat you.","done":"Me like fishy head!\nMe no eat you now.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":35.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Mudcrush Durtfeet","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"95737":{"id":95737,"t":"Seeking caitlin","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.","desc":"From time to time, I correspond with others in my craft--herbalists or eccentrics who study rare plants and local oddities. We trade discoveries, and sometimes warnings of what lies ahead.\nOne alchemist in the Wetlands wrote of an excavation team her husband was part of, uncovering signs of a long-lost primordial grass... but she never sent word of its abundance or accessibility.\nIf you can, check on Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.\nAshenvale Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":35,"y":48.4,"n":"Llana","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":11.8,"y":58.6,"n":"Caitlin Grassman","e":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"4297":{"id":4297,"t":"Food for Baby","lv":47,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Silvermane Stalker Flanks to Agnar Beastamer in Hinterlands.\n5 Silvermane Stalker Flank Silvermane Stalker 35 %","desc":"Sprite darters are omnivores--that means they eat both meat and vegetation. If your egg here's gonna hatch, we best be prepared. Some good eats for these little guys are flanks of meat, raw and juicy, believe it or not. I was never able to find out why, but it has somethin' to do with Elune's plan for the elves... maybe they were to be protectors or somethin', I don't know.\nI'll take care of the egg for now, why don't you get me some good Silvermane stalker flanks for 'em to eat when he's hatched.","rew":"Experience: 4,200\n+100 reputation with Darnassus\n+100 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"Find that meat yet, ‹name›? Your little egg here's just about ready to hatch. If he don't have a good enough first meal, then he might not make it past his first week, and I'd hate for that to happen.\nCan't much lie to ya, ‹name›. I'm jealous of you gettin' this egg to begin with. Don't make me regret helpin' ya out like this.","done":"These'll do nicely, and if I'm not mistaken, your little egg's just about ready to hatch. How does it feel? You know, you about to be a father/mother? Haha, didn't think ya'd have to deal with such responsibility, now did ya?","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":14.2,"y":43.6,"n":"Agnar Beastamer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"9337":{"id":9337,"t":"Major Mana Potion","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0.","obj":"15 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nMajor Mana Potion","back":"In addition to our other supplies, we also have a number of major mana potions you may find useful. I will give you one in exchange for fifteen necrotic runes.","done":"Here you are, ‹name›. Be careful out there. Our numbers are not so large we can afford many battlefield casualties.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.8,"y":30.7,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":72.6,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.1,"y":45.4,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"8937":{"id":8937,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Belt of Valor and a set of Gauntlets of Valor to Deliana in Ironforge.\nBelt of Valor Patchwork Horror 3.3 % in Stratholme , Venom Belcher 3 % in Stratholme , Bile Spewer 2.7 % in Stratholme , Smolderthorn Berserker 2 %\nGauntlets of Valor Ramstein the Gorger 12 %","desc":"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gauntlets that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","rew":"You will receive:\nBelt of Heroism Gauntlets of Heroism\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the trade?","done":"You've kept your end of the bargain, I shall keep mine.\nJust remember that I'm holding on to the best pieces until your work is finished.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2857":{"id":2857,"t":"Wild Leather Helmet","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Nightscape Tunics, 2 Nightscape Headbands, and a Wildvine to Jangdor Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\n2 Nightscape Tunic\n2 Nightscape Headband\nWildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"A Wild Leather helmet offers the wearer superior protection to the vital areas of the head without a sacrifice in comfort. As with all Wild Leather armor, the integrated wildvine yields a powerful but random magic imbuement to the helm's frame. Leather wearers will definitely want this piece!\nFor this pattern, I will need two Nightscape tunics, 2 Nightscape headbands, and a wildvine. Complete this lesson and the pattern will be yours!","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Helmet\nExperience: 2,900","back":"I need those tunics and headbands made, and I also need that piece of wildvine before I will share with you the knowledge of Wild Leather helmets.\nHead gear is highly coveted amongst adventurers, whether it be a disarmingly simple headband or a full-covering helmet. The fundamentals of creating valued head gear remain constant, no matter what the cosmetic appearance of the gear is.","done":"This Nightscape equipment you have supplied perfectly meets the requirements I have given to you, ‹name›. I expect no less from a leatherworker of your caliber.\nYou have earned the honor of crafting Wild Leather helmets. I give this pattern to you freely, and hope you will profit from it accordingly.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"9257":{"id":9257,"t":"Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 143,000, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris wants you to take Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian to Stratholme and use it on Consecrated Earth. Defeat the entity that is exorcised from the staff and return to him.\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian\nAtiesh Cleansed\nProvided: Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian","desc":"This final task will be the most difficult of all, ‹name›. You have faced and defeated both an Old God and the Lich King's General, but now you must face the hand of Sargeras.\nTake the staff to Stratholme. It is there that you will find a piece of consecrated earth: ground where the greatest knights of Lordaeron were murdered. Place the befouled staff upon the holy ground and prepare for an entity of immense power to break from within... Defeat the demonic being that controls the staff and return to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"217":{"id":217,"t":"In Defense of the King's Lands","lv":17,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill the Trogg leader, Grawmug, and his two guards, Gnasher and Brawler then report back to Captain Rugelfuss in the southern guard tower.\nGrawmug slain\nGnasher slain\nBrawler slain","desc":"‹name›, our scouts have identified the leader of this recent Trogg incursion. It appears that these beasts in Loch Modan are following the lead of a chieftain named Grawmug. Grawmug is heavily guarded, however. Two of his most elite guards, Gnasher and Brawler, never leave his side.\nIf you feel yourself worthy, ‹name›, I want you to lead the assassination mission on Grawmug and his two thugs. With the Trogg leadership dead, we just might stand a chance at pushing these beasts back into the ground.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFrontier Britches Dwarven Defender Lucky Trousers\nExperience: 1,600\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Grawmug and his two guards, Gnasher and Brawler, are still alive. Your mission is not complete until all 3 have been brought to death. The Dwarven empire is counting on you, ‹name›.","done":"Most excellent, ‹name›! You have brought hope to Loch Modan. With Grawmug dead, we stand a better chance of seeing the Troggs eliminated from the land.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":23.2,"y":73.7,"n":"Captain Rugelfuss","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"297":{"id":297,"t":"Gathering Idols","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Magmar Fellhew 8 Carved Stone Idols.\n8 Carved Stone Idol Berserk Trogg 80 % , Stonesplinter Digger 80 % , Stonesplinter Geomancer 80 %","desc":"Recently, just before the Troggs surfaced within the site, we had uncovered a large number of strange, carved idols. But we didn't have the chance to study them, for soon after their discovery the Troggs chased us away from the ruins! And those idols have a strange effect on the Troggs. It makes them go berserk!\nBring me 8 idols - I want to study them, and I want them out of Trogg hands! You can find the idols on the Troggs infesting the site.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDwarven Flamestick Trogg Slicer Thelsamar Axe\nExperience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you have those Idols? We must study them and report our findings to Ironforge!","done":"You got them! Nicely done, ‹name›!\nAnd you don't look too worse for wear, even with those berserk Troggs about. I'm going to keep my eye on you...you show some promise.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":64.9,"y":66.7,"n":"Magmar Fellhew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"9097":{"id":9097,"t":"Frostfire Circlet","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Frostfire Circlet if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Circlet, 15 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 3 Mooncloth and 3 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Circlet\n15 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n3 Mooncloth\n3 Nexus Crystal","desc":"As a Watcher, I was allowed access to many of Medivh's personal effects. Among those items, I found the tomes most enlightening. While the majority of the books were filled with - to put it bluntly - tripe, there were some gems. One of those tomes documented the creation of a set of armor fit for an archmage: Frostfire.\n<Angela points to her head.>\nIt's all in here and I am willing to share the fruits of that knowledge with you as long as you are able to provide me with the necessary materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostfire Circlet\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !,\nyou got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Frostfire Circlet.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9017":{"id":9017,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Beaststalker's Boots, Beaststalker's Pants and Beaststalker's Mantle.\nBeaststalker's Boots Nerub'enkan 0 % in Stratholme\nBeaststalker's Pants Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nBeaststalker's Mantle Overlord Wyrmthalak 0 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nBeastmaster's Boots Beastmaster's Pants Beastmaster's Mantle\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, ‹name›. Let us take care of your reward first.","done":"This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\nEastern Plaguelands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"3097":{"id":3097,"t":"Hallowed Scroll","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Hallowed Scroll and speak to Dark Cleric Duesten in the church in Deathknell.\nHallowed Scroll\nProvided: Hallowed Scroll","desc":"Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the priest trainer Duesten. I would take some time to read it before heading out again.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Ah, so between fire, plague, rioting, and much worse, one more of the \"faithful\" comes to my door. Well, let me bid you welcome, ‹class›. And allow me a moment to explain a thing or two before you decide it's time for you to seek whatever drives you forward: the Holy Light no longer concerns you, the spirits of your forefathers are fairy tales, and creatures from the Nether don't want you.\nDo you understand me so far?","done":"There is only one thing you must know: we have survived through will alone. It is faith in ourselves that separates us from others, and with our powers, we will cause great change in all of Azeroth. The weak will come to lean on you. The lepers will call you Lord. And the ignorant will look to you for guidance. It is my duty to make sure you have the necessary tools so when the time comes, you are prepared. As you grow in experience, seek me out. I will teach you greater powers if you are ready.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31.1,"y":66,"n":"Dark Cleric Duesten","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94777":{"id":94777,"t":"Divine grace","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, ‹race›. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Cathedral of Light. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.\nElune be with you, good ‹race›.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94777","cats":["priest"]},"5657":{"id":5657,"t":"Hex of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Home. Return home, young ‹race›.\nYour spiritual leader Ur'kyo begs you to return to him and speak about the path you travel.\nGo to the Valley of Spirits in the great Horde city of Orgrimmar. You will find him there.","rew":"You will learn: Hex of Weakness\nExperience: 210","done":"You would do well to pay heed to this lesson, young one. The Hex of Weakness will be a great boon to you in battle. Later I will have tests for you to further yourself and prove your worth to the tribe.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":68.8,"n":"Ken'jai","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"7737":{"id":7737,"t":"Gaining Acceptance","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Dark Iron Residue Burrowing Thundersnout 29.9 % , Dark Screecher 25.4 % , Borer Beetle 25.4 % , Twilight's Hammer Executioner 22.3 % and 4 more","back":"You've worked your way up through the Brotherhood's corporate hierarchy, ‹race›. We have begun to look favorably upon you. Quite an accomplishment!\nIf you're interested in more work and earning more respect amongst us, listen up.\nWe can refine the fiery flux by adding a simple Dark Iron residue to the mix. The Dark Iron residue can be found in Blackrock Depths.","done":"Keep the residue pouring in!","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.8,"y":28.5,"n":"Master Smith Burninate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"1657":{"id":1657,"t":"Stinking Up Southshore","lv":60,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Toss three Forsaken Stink Bombs into the heart of Southshore in Hillsbrad, and return to Darkcaller Yanka at the Wickerman Festival in Tirisfal Glade.\nToss Stink Bomb into Southshore : 0/ 3\nProvided: Forsaken Stink Bomb Cluster","desc":"Celebrate Hallow's End in style... by bringing grief to our enemies in Southshore!\nTake one of these specially crafted stink bombs. It is filled with an odiferous funk that no human - or any weak-willed beast for that matter - can stand to smell. You'll need to throw it right in the heart of Southshore for it to do its job, so be prepared for a fight against the Alliance!\nWhen you've completed this task... this tribute to our liberation, return to me!","rew":"You will receive:\n15 Hallow's End Pumpkin Treat\nExperience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you delivered our \"gift\" to the people of Southshore?\n<Darkcaller Yanka laughs wickedly.>","done":"Ah, well done! I hope the Alliance chokes on the foul gift we've given them, much like we were forced to choke on the yoke of enslavement to the Scourge!\nYou've kept the ideas of Hallow's End true, ‹name›, and for that I salute you. As an extra bonus, let me share some of these Hallow's End treats I have with you. I think you might find them to be quite the enjoyable diversion!\nTirisfal Glades Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":55.6,"y":69.9,"n":"Darkcaller Yanka","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"97257":{"id":97257,"t":"Call of fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Wait for Olariaan to begin the ritual at the Brazier of Offering and follow his instructions.\nYou must deliver the Eternal Flame to Valanaar before the timer runs out.\nComplete the Ritual with Olariaan\nLight the Brazier of Eternal Flame\nProvided: Torch of Eternal Flame","desc":"Now we will perform the ritual.\nI will place the materials onto the altar and call forth the spirits of flame. If the offering is accepted, they will appear and light the Eternal Flame. You will then hold your torch forth and capture the flame.\nCarry the lit torch to Valanaar and place it in the Brazier of Eternal Flames. You must do so quickly, for the flames of the Firelands are quick to dissipate here in Skywall.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Totem Totem of Charged Flames\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 1,050\n+25 reputation with Windshapers","back":"You have done well to come this far. You do the Windshapers honor, Bilbøn.","done":"It is done. The Eternal Flame burns once again.\nYour trial is now complete. I am pleased to present you with your Fire Totem. Use this icon of power well in your travels, Bilbøn.\nJust remember, the power of the elemental plane serves those that respect it, and consumes those who do not. This is our way.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":51.2,"y":86,"n":"Olariaan Swiftburn","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":58.2,"y":78.4,"n":"Sessaria Skystride","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8377":{"id":8377,"t":"Armaments of War","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Reservist's Legguards Desertstalkers's Gauntlets\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"War comes, ‹name›, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.\nShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...\n<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>\nThe future of us all could be at an end.\nThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8537":{"id":8537,"t":"Crimson Templar","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Summon and slay a Crimson Templar and report back to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing II in order to complete this quest.\nTactical Task Briefing II\nCrimson Templar slain\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing II","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer and the elemental nobles they worship present a formidable threat to our operations in Silithus. With the new enemies we're facing inside Ahn'Qiraj, we cannot afford to lower our guard to our enemies outside.\nFind a way to summon and destroy a Crimson Templar and report to Bor Wildmane.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Is your task done yet, ‹name›?","done":"Good job, ‹name›. Here's your next assignment.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8857":{"id":8857,"t":"Secrets of the Colossus - Ashi","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Colossus of Ashi's Husk to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.\nColossus of Ashi's Husk\nProvided: Colossus of Ashi's Husk","desc":"I'm looking for battle hardened adventurers willing and able to get a fresh husk sample from the fallen Colossus of Ashi to Oglethorpe in Booty Bay. No, no, I wouldn't want you to go anywhere near that thing's corpse. Just take one of my samples and make it snappy. These things are no good to him rotten!","rew":"You will receive:\nColossal Bag of Loot\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Booty Bay\n+200 reputation with Booty Bay\n+200 reputation with Booty Bay\n+200 reputation with Booty Bay","back":"Yes? What have you got there?","done":"Oh the chickens I will craft from this wondrous husk! Well done, my boy/girl !\nSilithus Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.5,"y":37.3,"n":"Colossus Researcher Nestor","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8777":{"id":8777,"t":"Target: Hive'Regal Burrowers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 30 Hive'Regal Burrowers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing XI in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing XI\nHive'Regal Burrower slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing XI","desc":"As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations. You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Regal where your primary target will consist of Hive'Regal burrowers.\nReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You wish to tell me something, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Your part in the attack on Hive'Regal has been noted.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"79097":{"id":79097,"t":"Baxtan on destructive magics","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Baxtan: On Destructive Magics","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nBaxtan: On Destructive Magics (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1097":{"id":1097,"t":"Elmore's Task","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Grimand Elmore.","desc":"There's a dwarven weaponsmith in Stormwind, Grimand Elmore, who sent word that he needs help with a delivery. I believe he wants a package sent to his homeland in the north.\nYou have a sturdy pair on you! So if you're interested in some legwork then speak with Grimand. We could use you down here, but we must also keep our ties strong with the dwarves.\nYou can find Grimand Elmore at the weapon shop in the Dwarven District of Stormwind, in the northeast section of town.","rew":"Experience: 110","done":"You're here to help with my delivery? Very good!\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":65.5,"n":"Smith Argus","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"7497":{"id":7497,"t":"The Journey Has Just Begun","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will learn: Onyxia Scale Cloak","done":"A dragon slayer and a seasoned leatherworker? You do not cease to astonish, hero. I am humbled.\nPlease accept what I am about to teach you. This knowledge will prove to be invaluable if you are to destroy what remains of the Black Dragonflight.\nCreate the cloak from the scales of the brood mother. It will protect you and your allies against the incendiary breath of the Lord of Blackrock... Nefarian.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.2,"y":85.5,"n":"Major Mattingly","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"617":{"id":617,"t":"Akiris by the Bundle","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Bundles of Akiris Reed to Privateer Bloads in Booty Bay.\n10 Akiris Reed Naga Explorer 30 %","desc":"You looking fer work, ‹name›? I might have some if you're up for a little challenge.\nI got a friend named Groy who makes a killing selling what the naga call akiris reed: it's some kind of valuable ocean reed. Not too sure what it's for, but he pays well for bundles of the stuff.\nYa bring me ten stalks of the stuff, and we'll have business to do. The naga were last seen along the beach to the north of here.","rew":"You will receive:\nScorching Sash\nMoney: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"If ya got no business with me, then move along, ‹name›.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. 10 stalks of akiris reed wasn't too much a challenge after all, huh? No offense to the naga, but hey, everybody's gotta make a living.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.8,"y":76.4,"n":"Privateer Bloads","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8057":{"id":8057,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Haruspex's Bracers","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Stanchion. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nMaywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Stanchion\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"A haruspex is a key member of our tribe; you'll be wise to listen to their portents. By communion with animals and givin' them up to the spirits when needed, they give us divine guidance. In times past, the haruspex's insight and wisdom gave us an edge in the wars against the splintered tribes of the Gurubashi.\nBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us. Do this, and I'll give ya bracers that any haruspex of the Zandalar would want.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Haruspex's Bracers\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Have ya got the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub? These bracers are worth the effort, ‹name›. Trust me mon!","done":"Ah, I can sense the power comin' from these Paragons of Power, ‹name›. Ya proved to be someone we in the tribe can call \"friend.\" A deal is a deal, ‹name›... behold the power of the haruspex's bracers!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"97977":{"id":97977,"t":"Natures call","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 4 Gnarlpine Totems and bring them to Tarindrella.\n4 Gnarlpine Totem","desc":"The Gnarlpine furbolg would not turn on their ancient allies so readily. We must learn more of their plight.\nSearch their abandoned homes for totems. If any survived the chaos of their departure, their engravings may tell us more of what happened here.\nYou'll find their camps along the western edge of the glen, though the grell and grellkin may have scattered them beyond.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 0 silver, 50 copper Experience: 250\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Don't worry about any larger totems you might find. I wouldn't know what to do with them if you found a way to get them!","done":"Oh, it's even worse than I thought.\nThese engravings tell us that the Gnarlpine began having nightmares of being wiped out by some great shadow. Before long, that fear turned to rage--and the shadow to their former elven friends. To be aware of your own mind slipping away from you...\nOur only hope is that this may help us better understand what is happening on Teldrassil. Thank you for your aid, Django.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.8,"y":45,"n":"Tarindrella","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"457":{"id":457,"t":"The Balance of Nature","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Conservator Ilthalaine needs you to kill 7 Mangy Nightsabers and 7 Thistle Boars.\nMangy Nightsaber slain : 0/ 7\nThistle Boar slain : 0/ 7","desc":"Thinning the younger population of creatures here in Shadowglen was a good start, ‹name›, but there is still work to be done.\nThe resources of the forest will be depleted too quickly if the problem is not addressed. Killing nature's beasts is a necessary evil for the good of all who share the land. Venture into the forest and slay mangy nightsabers and thistle boars in the name of balance.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDraped Cloak Blackened Leather Belt\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 0 silver, 50 copper Experience: 250\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Your task is not yet complete, ‹name›. Return to me once 7 mangy nightsabers and 7 thistle boars have been killed.","done":"You have proven your dedication to nature well, ‹name›. A young ‹class› like yourself has a promising future.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":44.3,"n":"Conservator Ilthalaine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"937":{"id":937,"t":"The Enchanted Glade","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 6 Bloodfeather Belts and bring them to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade.\n6 Bloodfeather Belt Bloodfeather Matriarch 33 % , Bloodfeather Wind Witch 33 % , Bloodfeather Fury 33 % , Bloodfeather Sorceress 33 % and 3 more","desc":"I was dispatched with a small group of Sentinels here to protect the Oracle Tree from the harpies that have made nests all around the glade. Little by little we are trying to push them back.\nWhen the Oracle Tree attempted to send a runner to Darnassus with a report, the messenger was attacked and killed by a group of the harpies.\nIf you feel up to the task, go to their nests, slay them, and return their belts to me as proof of your deeds.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShackled Girdle Rain-spotted Cape\nExperience: 440\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Their slashing talons and piercing beaks may prove a difficult match for your own abilities, ‹name›, but I have faith that you will not fail in this task.","done":"I am impressed by what you have accomplished here in so short a time, ‹name›. Would that I could ask you to remain here to assist me with my duties... but I know in my heart that greater tasks lie ahead for you.\nI have noticed the Oracle Tree has just shed a piece of its bark. No doubt it has a task that it wishes completed. You should speak with it.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":38.3,"y":34.4,"n":"Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"857":{"id":857,"t":"The Tear of the Moons","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Feegly the Exiled wants you to retrieve for him the Tear of the Moons.\nTear of the Moons General Twinbraid's Strongbox","desc":"The power was mine! In my very hands! And I want it back! Back I say!\nThose dirty excavators uncovered it... so beautiful it was. Deemed the Tear of the Moons, it was the first great discovery we made at Bael Modan.\nIt should have been mine! Mine I say!\nGeneral Twinbraid grew jealous of the power it gave me. He locked it away in the Keep. Called it cursed, he did! The fool!\nOthers wanted it and they had to be stopped! That bastard Twinbraid drove me off.\nNow I want it back. Back I say!","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450","back":"Where is the Tear of the Moons? I need it now! Need I say!","done":"At last, the power is mine again! Mine I say!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":49,"y":86.3,"n":"Feegly the Exiled","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2937":{"id":2937,"t":"Summoning Shadra","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat Shadra at the altar of Shadra'Alor, then bring her venom to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\nShadra's Venom Shadra\nProvided: Gadrin's Parchment","desc":"Take his parchment, and read it at the altar of Shadra'Alor, deep within the witherbark realm in the Hinterlands. This will summon Shadra the spider god.","rew":"Experience: 8,450\n+200 reputation with Undercity","back":"Did you get the venom?","done":"Sweet, you got it!\nDurotar Hillsbrad Foothills The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.9,"y":74.7,"n":"Master Gadrin","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"377":{"id":377,"t":"Crime and Punishment","lv":26,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,400 experience instead of 2,100, 2.1 times as much. New rewards: Town Clerk's Mittens. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a","obj":"Councilman Millstipe of Darkshire wants you to bring him the hand of Dextren Ward.\nHand of Dextren Ward Dextren Ward","desc":"As if the neglect for the residents of Duskwood was not bad enough, now the House of Nobles spits in the eye of the Darkshire Council with their decision to imprison Dextren Ward in Stormwind rather than behead the villain as per Lord Ebonlocke's sentence.\nWard was caught selling bodies from the cemetery to Morbent Fel, a crime punishable by death. Yet Stormwind claims Ward as their prisoner.\nAssassinate Ward in The Stormwind Stockade - bring me his hand - and I shall reward you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAmbassador's Boots Darkshire Mail Leggings Town Clerk's Mittens\nNew in Forever: Town Clerk's Mittens.\nExperience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"So long as a molester of the dead like Dextren Ward is permitted to live, justice stands betrayed. Return to me once Lord Ebonlocke's sentence of death is carried out on that defiler, Ward. We shall give the families of the dead the closure they deserve and better yet, we will send a clear message to the House of Nobles in Stormwind.","done":"So Dextren Ward finally paid for his crimes against humanity? Good riddance to the scum I say. And cheers to you, my friend! Not only have you given the families of the dead the peace of mind they deserve, you sent a poignant message to those corrupt bureaucrats in the House of Nobles. Stormwind must rise to the needs of the people of Duskwood or we will break free from their tyranny.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":71.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Councilman Millstipe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-stockade"]},"7817":{"id":7817,"t":"A Donation of Mageweave","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. Such generosity would not go unnoticed by the Undercity, I assure you!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":71.7,"y":29.2,"n":"Ralston Farnsley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"5097":{"id":5097,"t":"All Along the Watchtowers","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Beacon Torch, mark each tower in Andorhal; you will need to stand in the doorway of the tower to successfully mark it.\nOnce all four towers are marked, return the Beacon Torch to Commander Ashlam Valorfist in Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\nTower One marked\nTower Two marked\nTower Three marked\nTower Four marked\nProvided: Beacon Torch","desc":"Through the use of a magical device known as a beacon torch, we can mark targets of our choosing for future actions by our troops. To that end, we think the Scourge are using Andorhal's watchtowers as a means to control their troop movements.\nYour mission: breach Andorhal's defenses to plant beacons at all four watchtowers. You'll need to be in the doorway of each tower to plant the beacon; it will then proceed to mark the tower. There are only five charges on the beacon torch, so use them wisely!","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Once the towers are marked, they'll become top priority targets for our attack on Andorhal. I suspect that once we neutralize the towers, the main threat of Andorhal will emerge. From that point on, we'll have a straight-up fight for control of the city!\nyou're back to report success, yes? Don't forget the beacon torch as well; we must maintain control of our materiel.","done":"My priests are reporting that our beacon trackers are picking up extremely strong signals on all four towers! Dare I say it, but I believe you've executed another mission with complete and total success! Well played once again, ‹name›!\nWith the towers marked, our preparations for the attack are now in place. The time has come to take the fight to the Scourge!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"98297":{"id":98297,"t":"Stopping the cycle","lv":34,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill the Subdued Dragonspawn at the Dragonmaw Gates for Howin Kindfeather.\nSubdued Dragonspawn slain","desc":"I did a quick test flight while ye were out. The good news is the armor ye helped me craft for Bassbeak works like a charm!\nThe very bad news is I saw a group o' them Dragonmaw in the process of enslavin' a red dragonspawn.\nAbsolutely not. Not again.\nYou have tae take it out. You'll certainly need friends tae do so. Kill the warlocks holding it down first--that ought tae free it. Then put it out of its misery.\nNone of them will stand in the way of the Wildhammer.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFallen Dragon's Scepter Trusty Sword Subdued Dragon's Fang\nExperience: 2,700\n+150 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.4,"y":42,"n":"Howin Kindfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"93737":{"id":93737,"t":"The broken construct","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Rianni Nightwind and list to what he has to say.\nListen to what Riaani Nightwind has to say\nCrystallized Lightning\nEnchanted Gyrozephyr\nAir Construct Core","desc":"Oh, hello. Ayessa sent you to assist me? Very well then.\nNot sure what an obvious novice like yourself can do, but if you give me a moment to pull my head out of this construct's innards I might have a few ideas of things you can do to help.","back":"I can't imagine why anyone would want to steal these components from this construct. Other than the gyrozephyr these components have almost no practical application. Even the gyro would be nigh-useless outside of its intended purpose.","done":"Thank you for scavenging these materials. I imagine that some of this wasn't terribly easy to get.\nWith these parts I can get the construct up and running again. From there we can just hope that its memory is intact and it can tell us who took its components.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":73,"n":"Riaani Nightwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});